## Test-block Flow Rate

The above design mass flow rate, which reflects the heater's combustion-air requirements at design conditions (with maximum hot-air recycle, as applicable), should be multiplied by a test-block flow factor to obtain the test block mass flow rate. For typical APH-system applications, a test-block flow factor (Ftbf) of 1.15 (115 %) is recommended. This 1,15 test-block flow factor accounts for the following:

a) inaccuracies in the calculation of the heater's air requirements;

inaccuracies and/or potential increases in the exchanger's leakage rate;

inaccuracies in the FD fan's rating/sizing correlations;

changes in the fuel composition(s) and/or excess-air percentages;

